         <notesStmt>
            <note type="project" target="#dat1">This draft was probably prepared for the printing of a proof slip prior to the poem's first publication in 1887, as one of the notes at the top appears to have been written by a person engaged in setting the poem in type. The glue marks on this and another manuscript (nyp.00051) align, indicating that Whitman had written the lines on the latter as a revision of the last three lines in the present manuscript.</note>
            <note type="work_relations" target="xxx.00368" cert="high">"You Lingering Sparse Leaves of Me" was first published in the November 1887 issue of <hi rend="italic">Lippincott's Magazine</hi>. There, the poem was part of a four-poem sequence titled "November Boughs." That grouping was not maintained when the poem was further revised and printed in <hi rend="italic">November Boughs</hi> (1888) and in the "Sands at Seventy" annex to <hi rend="italic">Leaves of Grass</hi> (1891-1892).
            </note>
